# A VM per platform

Stowage keeps no state of a VM: an OpenTofu root of yours makes it, with the platform's own
provider, from `stowage_vm_seed`, and `stowage_vm_install` installs and keeps it. Each platform has
a complete root in the provider's repository, `examples/guides/<platform>-vm/`: copy it into your
own root. Each README lists its resources' import IDs, for a VM made by Stowage 0.39.0 or earlier
(`vm create --create opentofu`, whose state Stowage reads no more).

